===''Wake Up''===
[[File:Hoopa Surprise Ring Adventures short 2.png|thumb|250px|Screenshot from ''Wake Up'']]
'''Wake Up''' (Japanese: '''めざまし''' ''Alarm Clock'') is the second animated short. It first aired in Japan on April 30, 2015 and in the United States on December 11, 2015.

====Summary====
One morning, {{Ash}} and {{AP|Pikachu}} sleep through several alarms that are set to go off at 6:45am. {{an|Hoopa}} then summons {{p|Loudred}}, {{p|Exploud}}, and {{p|Noivern}} who use their [[Sound-based move|sound-based attacks]] to wake Ash, creating a shockwave that sends the tent flying. Pikachu, still asleep, then accidentally uses {{m|Thunderbolt}} on Ash and Hoopa.

====Characters====
=====Humans=====
* {{Ash}}

=====Pokémon=====
* {{p|Pikachu}} ({{OP|Ash|Pikachu}})
* {{p|Hoopa}} ({{an|Hoopa|anime}})
* {{p|Noivern}}
* {{p|Loudred}}
* {{p|Exploud}}

====Errors====
* When Ash and his Pikachu are still sleeping on their tent at 6:45am, one of the Exploud alarm clock's eyes are colored white instead of pink.

===''Ball Pickup''===
[[File:Hoopa Surprise Ring Adventures short 3.png|thumb|250px|Screenshot from ''Ball Pickup'']]
'''Ball Pickup''' (Japanese: '''たまひろい''' ''Ball Boy'') is the third animated short. It first aired in Japan on May 7, 2015 and in the United States on December 11, 2015.

====Summary====
{{Ash}} and his {{AP|Hawlucha}} are {{pkmn|training}}. Ash throws {{i|Poké Ball}}s at Hawlucha and Hawlucha kicks them back. {{an|Hoopa}} provides the Poké Balls by letting them appear through portals. However, suddenly a {{p|Voltorb}} appears from one of the portals. It hits Ash, and when Hoopa starts laughing, Voltorb attacks it. Voltorb then uses {{m|Self-Destruct}}, leaving Ash, Pikachu, Hawlucha, and Hoopa deep fried.

====Characters====
=====Humans=====
* {{Ash}}

=====Pokémon=====
* {{p|Pikachu}} ({{OP|Ash|Pikachu}})
* {{p|Hawlucha}} ({{OP|Ash|Hawlucha}})
* {{p|Hoopa}} ({{an|Hoopa|anime}})
* {{p|Voltorb}}

====Trivia====
* This is the only short to feature one of {{cat|Ash's Pokémon}} other than Pikachu.
* In the English dub, Voltorb has the cry of an {{p|Electrode}}.

===''Heated Battle''===
[[File:Hoopa Surprise Ring Adventures short 4.png|thumb|250px|Screenshot from ''Heated Battle'']]
'''Heated Battle''' (Japanese: '''あついバトル''' ''Hot Battle'') is the fourth animated short. It first aired in Japan on May 14, 2015 and in the United States on December 11, 2015.

====Summary====
{{Ash}} and {{AP|Pikachu}} are facing off in a boxing ring. Suddenly, {{an|Hoopa}} appears and summons a {{p|Blaziken}}. Seeing this, Ash and Pikachu get more fired up than they already were. Because of that, Hoopa starts to summon more {{type|Fire}} Pokémon. It summons a {{p|Slugma}}, a {{p|Rapidash}}, a {{p|Magmortar}} and a {{p|Heatran}}, who use their Fire-type moves to set Ash and Pikachu on fire. They start running around with fire on their tails and Hoopa laughs at them. Then, out of nowhere, Hoopa is roasted with another Fire-type attack. It falls down to the ground as the Pokémon who did this, a {{p|Moltres}}, flies by.

